# The Hall of Fame (FameWin), which the game shows at a game's end and no click reaches: opened with the script host's "open"
# step on the loaded first turn (final = 0, so it only shows the list: the file in the game folder holds one game). The window
# as it opens; the mouse over a portrait; a portrait chosen with no game of its faction (the empty list) and one with the game;
# a click on a place in the list; each of the six record buttons; Escape (closes). The state regions are the list of games
# (the file's 0x1324 bytes) and the window object's working numbers, the game shown, the chosen portrait, the panels and the looks of the six record buttons. Leave time after each step; the snaps take 2 s each.
25 load
42 state fame 0x9a3840 0x1324
42 state work 0x74e50c 0x3c
42 state sel 0x758410 4
42 state group 0x7534e8 0x10
42 state rects 0x758f24 0x60
42 state btn0 0x753fb4 4
42 state btn1 0x754b00 4
42 state btn2 0x75564c 4
42 state btn3 0x756198 4
42 state btn4 0x756ce4 4
42 state btn5 0x757830 4
42 snap map
44 open hall_of_fame
50 snap fame
52 move 620 258
56 snap hover-portrait
58 click 300 258        # a portrait whose faction has no game
62 snap portrait-empty
64 click 192 258
68 snap portrait-first
70 click 280 440        # a place with no game
74 snap place-empty
76 click 280 380        # the place with the game
80 snap place-game
82 click 248 160        # the six record buttons
86 snap record-0
88 click 355 160
92 snap record-1
94 click 465 160
98 snap record-2
100 click 572 160
104 snap record-3
106 click 680 160
110 snap record-4
112 click 787 160
116 snap record-5
118 move 775 647        # over OK
122 snap hover-ok
124 key Escape
128 snap map-after
132 close
